{"skill":{"slug":"local-whisper","displayName":"Local Whisper"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1769159934671,"changelog":"- Initial release of local-whisper: local speech-to-text using OpenAI Whisper, fully offline after model download.\n- Supports multiple model sizes for different speed/quality needs: tiny, base (default), small, turbo, large-v3.\n- Includes options for language selection, timestamps, JSON output, and quiet mode.\n- Provides clear setup instructions using uv-managed Python virtual environment.\n- Requires ffmpeg for audio processing.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1386,"sha256":"bb27c6bcee9c5bbc1f3467b1112e89afe5bd4cb1050b50e89fa4badf721e1622","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/transcribe.py","size":2511,"sha256":"ced1a448a8e888e1d442466c745e24ea42a5ac8a66a06aa292b29fc45f3e5fbc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1921,"sha256":"0e073296cce2144ae68fc059e605fba84e9c54fd93ed6f8b0c6d184b94314ad8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789017275761,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9ae811382a50c116fa5d6530e06eb2928c57b1448fa09921a9b26796f581cc86","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9ae811382a50c116fa5d6530e06eb2928c57b1448fa09921a9b26796f581cc86","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: local-whisper\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides local speech-to-text functionality using OpenAI Whisper. The `SKILL.md` clearly outlines its purpose, usage, and setup, including legitimate dependencies like `ffmpeg` and Python libraries `openai-whisper` and `torch` from trusted sources (download.pytorch.org). The `scripts/transcribe.py` script correctly implements the transcription logic without any signs of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection against the agent. The only network activity is the expected initial download of Whisper models by the `openai-whisper` library, which is consistent with the 'offline after model download' description.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159847845},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789017275761},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward local audio transcription helper with a normal dependency-installation caution.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill needs ffmpeg, local model files, and access to the chosen audio file, which is proportionate for offline transcription after the initial model download.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Setup uses a uv-managed .venv and installs click, openai-whisper, and torch from a documented HTTPS package index, but the dependencies are not pinned or hash-locked.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime behavior is narrow and user-directed, but the usage examples reference scripts/local-whisper while the inspected artifact contains scripts/transcribe.py; this looks like a packaging/usability mismatch rather than hidden security behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No services, startup hooks, credential access, memory writes, privilege escalation, destructive actions, or cross-session backdoors were found; persistence is limited to the skill files, virtual environment, and normal model cache behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is local Whisper speech-to-text, and the bundled script loads a selected Whisper model, transcribes a user-provided audio file, and prints text or JSON output.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install it as an unprivileged user, expect a large initial model/dependency download, and consider pinning or reviewing package versions if you need reproducible or tightly controlled installs.","findings":"[T08] expected: The static scan warning about unpinned dependencies is valid as a supply-chain hardening issue, but dependency installation is disclosed, isolated to a virtual environment, and directly required for the skill's transcription purpose.\n[SkillSpector] expected: SkillSpector reported no issues; independent inspection likewise found no prompt hijacking, data exfiltration, persistence, or unrelated high-impact behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789017275761}}}}}